            <div xml:id="d517">

                <pb facs="0508" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">713.1311/248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-02-17T09:00:00-05:45">February 17, 1934—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>55. My 51, February 16, noon.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d517-f1"/> The President
                    showed me yesterday telegram sent last night to Ubico requesting latter to
                    accede to slight postponement requested by Costa Rica.</p>
                <p>Private secretary has just telephoned me that Ubico’s reply states that
                    arrangement will be acceptable to Guatemala.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Central American mission[s].</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
